      <h1 id="oadp-self-service-troubleshooting" class="group scroll-mt-20">OADP Self-Service troubleshooting<a href="#oadp-self-service-troubleshooting" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p class="_abstract">Resolve common errors and issues when using OADP Self-Service by following troubleshooting procedures for backup storage locations and backup operations. This helps you quickly identify and fix problems independently.</p>
      <h2 id="oadp-self-service-troubleshoot-nabsl-same-ns_oadp-self-service-troubleshooting" class="group scroll-mt-20">Resolving error NonAdminBackupStorageLocation not found in the namespace<a href="#oadp-self-service-troubleshoot-nabsl-same-ns_oadp-self-service-troubleshooting" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">Resolve the <code>NonAdminBackupStorageLocation not found in the namespace</code> error by using a backup storage location that belongs to the same namespace as your backup. This helps ensure successful backup operations.</p>
      <p>Consider the following scenario of a namespace <code>admin</code> backup:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>You have created two <code>NonAdminBackupStorageLocations</code> (NABLs) custom resources (CRs) in two different namespaces, for example, <code>nabsl-1</code> in <code>namespace-1</code> and <code>nabsl-2</code> in <code>namespace-2</code>.</li>
      <li>You are taking a backup of <code>namespace-1</code> and use <code>nabsl-2</code> in the <code>NonAdminBackup</code> (NAB) CR.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>In this scenario, after creating the NAB CR, you get the following error. The cause of the error is that the NABSL CR does not belong to the namespace that you are trying to back up.</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: oadp.openshift.io/v1alpha1\nkind: NonAdminBackup\n...\nstatus:\n  conditions:\n  - lastTransitionTime: \"2025-02-20T10:13:00Z\"\n  message: 'NonAdminBackupStorageLocation not found in the namespace: NonAdminBackupStorageLocation.oadp.openshift.io\n    \"nabsl2\" not found'\n  reason: InvalidBackupSpec\n  status: \"False\"\n  type: Accepted\n  phase: BackingOff"} lang="yaml" />
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      Use the NABSL that belongs to the same namespace that you are trying to back up.
      <p>In this scenario, you must use <code>nabsl-1</code> in the NAB CR to back up <code>namespace-1</code>.</p>
      </li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="oadp-self-service-troubleshoot-nabsl-default_oadp-self-service-troubleshooting" class="group scroll-mt-20">Resolving error NonAdminBackupStorageLocation cannot be set as default<a href="#oadp-self-service-troubleshoot-nabsl-default_oadp-self-service-troubleshooting" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">Resolve the error that occurs when you set a <code>NonAdminBackupStorageLocation</code> (NABSL) custom resource (CR) as the default backup storage location. This helps you resolve validation errors and configure backup storage locations correctly.</p>
      <p>As a non-admin user, if you have created a NABSL CR in your authorized namespace, you cannot set the NABSL CR as the default backup storage location.</p>
      <p>If you set the NABSL CR as the default backup storage location, the NABSL CR fails to validate and the <code>NonAdminController</code> (NAC) gives an error message.</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"NonAdminBackupStorageLocation cannot be used as a default BSL"} lang="text" />
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      To successfully validate and reconcile the NABSL CR, set the <code>default</code> field to <code>false</code> in the NABSL CR:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: oadp.openshift.io/v1alpha1\nkind: NonAdminBackupStorageLocation\n...\nspec:\n  backupStorageLocationSpec:\n    credential:\n      key: cloud\n      name: cloud-credentials-gcp\n    default: false\n    objectStorage:\n      bucket: oad..7l8\n      prefix: velero\n    provider: gcp"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>where:</p>
      <dl class="my-4 space-y-2">
      <dt class="font-semibold"><code>default</code></dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground"><p>Specifies that the <code>default</code> backup storage location is set to <code>false</code>.</p></dd>
      </dl>
      </li>
      </ul>
